course: dictionary
lesson: 13698
title: Old words and false friends
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Insensible is a formal, old-fashioned word, so you will mostly meet it in old stories and grown-up writing. It has several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one is meant. It is also a false friend: it looks like sensible, but it does not mean the opposite of sensible. The opposite of sensible would be silly.
explain: «The boxer was knocked insensible in the third round.» Knocked is the clue. Someone knocked out is not awake or aware of anything, so insensible means unconscious here. «The gardener was insensible to the rain and worked on for hours.» The word to is the clue. Insensible to something means not aware of it, or not bothered by it.
explain: «Sam's fingers were so cold that they became insensible.» Here insensible means not able to feel anything. Try your meaning in the sentence: fingers that cannot feel the cold still make sense. Always check the words after insensible, such as to, and the words before it, such as knocked. They show you the meaning.
fact: Insensible means unconscious, not awake or aware.
fact: Insensible to something means not aware of it, or not affected by it, as in «insensible to the cold».
fact: Insensible does not mean the opposite of sensible. Sensible means wise and careful, so do not mix them up.
fact: In old writing, «by insensible degrees» means so slowly and gradually that you hardly notice the change.
fact: Insensible is formal, so it is used more in books and old stories than in everyday talk.
exercise: «The guard was knocked insensible by the blow.» What does insensible mean? | Full of feeling | Angry and loud | *Unconscious, not awake or aware | Very sensible and wise
exercise: «He played in the snow for hours, insensible to the cold.» What does insensible mean here? | *Not aware of the cold, or not bothered by it | Sensible about the weather | Very cold and shivering | Warm and cosy
exercise: Mia says insensible means the opposite of sensible. What is the right answer? | *No, it is a false friend and does not mean the opposite of sensible | Yes, it means silly | It means very wise and careful | It means very loud
test: «The doctor said the patient was insensible after the fall.» What does insensible mean? | Wise and careful | Very hungry | Happy and smiling | *Unconscious, not awake
test: «The change came by insensible degrees, so nobody noticed it at first.» What does insensible mean in «by insensible degrees»? | Very sensible and careful | Painful and sudden | *So slow and small that it is hard to notice | Very loud and fast
exam: Choose the meaning of insensible in «knocked insensible». | Sensible and wise | *Unconscious, not awake | Noisy and bright | Very hungry
